    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/agent/telemetry_index.py the per-job tier choice treats any tier file, raw or minute, with no parseable row as absent, so the choice falls through raw to minute to hour past every such file. A test in tests/test_telemetry_index.py asserts that a job with no raw file, a minute file holding only a blank line and an unparseable line, and an hour file with rows is answered from hour with the hour totals. The existing raw fall-through tests still pass. Gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_telemetry_index.py tests/test_telemetry_ingest.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status; any evidence fragment written ends with a trailing newline",
